14:46:26.441 [main] WARN dev.langchain4j.service.ToolErrorHandlingNotice -- AI Service 'io.github.mbcc.CopilotService$Agent' is configured with tools, but tool error handlers are not configured explicitly. The current default behavior is:
  - an error in the arguments generated by the LLM fails the AI Service invocation
  - an exception thrown by a tool is sent to the LLM as the message of that exception
Usually, the message of an exception is written for developers, not for the LLM: it can expose internal application details (file paths, SQL, credentials embedded in error messages, responses of downstream services) to the LLM provider, to the chat memory and to whoever can see the output of the AI Service.
These defaults are planned to change in an upcoming release. To avoid a breaking change when that happens, we recommend specifying error handlers explicitly.
Recommended (this is also the behavior the defaults are planned to change to):
  .toolArgumentsErrorHandler(ToolArgumentsErrorHandler.sendExceptionMessageToLlm()) // the LLM sees what went wrong and can retry with corrected arguments
  .toolExecutionErrorHandler(ToolExecutionErrorHandler.failInvocationUnlessVisibleToLlm()) // only exceptions written for the LLM reach it, everything else fails the invocation
With the recommended setting, a tool tells the LLM about a failure by throwing an exception that implements dev.langchain4j.exception.ToolErrorVisibleToLlm, for example:
  throw ToolErrorVisibleToLlm.from("There is no order with this ID.");
To keep the current behavior:
  .toolArgumentsErrorHandler(ToolArgumentsErrorHandler.failInvocation())
  .toolExecutionErrorHandler(ToolExecutionErrorHandler.sendExceptionMessageToLlm())
Other options are described in https://docs.langchain4j.dev/tutorials/tools#error-handling
This message is logged once per JVM. To turn it off, set the log level of the 'dev.langchain4j.service.ToolErrorHandlingNotice' logger to OFF.
